TITLE:: ZMorph
summary:: Original Digital Multiresonant Filter Response Morphing
categories:: UGens>Filters
related:: Guides/Filtra, Classes/Wasp, Classes/Steiner, Classes/Polivoks

DESCRIPTION::
ZMorph is an original digital multiresonant filter that smoothly morphs between complex spectral profiles. Inspired by the Z-plane filter concept originally pioneered by Dave Rossum and E-mu Systems, this is a clean-room digital implementation using original acoustic and synthetic filter configurations (containing no proprietary ROM, presets, or code).

Each filter shape consists of a parallel bank of four 2nd-order Topology-Preserving Transform (TPT) state-variable peaking/bandpass resonators combined with a direct passband path. ZMorph processes Shape A and Shape B in parallel and performs an equal-gain response crossfade:
teletype::
y[n] = (1 - \text{morph}) \cdot y_A[n] + \text{morph} \cdot y_B[n]
::
This response-domain morphing guarantees unconditional stability across all continuous sweeps, completely eliminating the recursive coefficient divergence and transient explosions associated with interpolating high-order IIR poles directly.

TABLE::
## Shape ID || Name || Description
## 0 || VowelA || Formant profile for open vowel "Ah" (730 Hz, 1090 Hz, 2440 Hz, 3500 Hz)
## 1 || VowelI || Formant profile for bright front vowel "Ee" (270 Hz, 2290 Hz, 3010 Hz, 4200 Hz)
## 2 || VowelU || Formant profile for deep back vowel "Oo" (300 Hz, 870 Hz, 2250 Hz, 3100 Hz)
## 3 || DeepComb || Comb filtering with alternating resonant peaks and destructive phase notches
## 4 || MetallicBell || Inharmonic resonant chime modes (440 Hz, 980 Hz, 1790 Hz, 3280 Hz)
## 5 || AcousticBody || Warm low-frequency wooden resonator body (110 Hz, 220 Hz, 450 Hz, 900 Hz)
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar

ARGUMENT:: in
Audio-rate input signal.

ARGUMENT:: morph
Continuous morph parameter in the range [0.0, 1.0].
When morph = 0.0, the output equals Shape A exactly.
When morph = 1.0, the output equals Shape B exactly.
Between 0.0 and 1.0, the filter smoothly interpolates the complex spectral response.
Supports both audio rate (.ar) and control rate (.kr) modulation.

ARGUMENT:: shapeA
Integer preset index for Shape A (init-only, range 0 to 5, default 0).

ARGUMENT:: shapeB
Integer preset index for Shape B (init-only, range 0 to 5, default 1).

returns:: An audio-rate filtered signal.

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
// Boot server
s.boot;

// 1. Slow vocal vowel morph: /A/ ("Ah") to /I/ ("Ee")
(
x = {
    var src = Saw.ar([110, 110.5]) * 0.25;
    var morph = SinOsc.kr(0.2).range(0.0, 1.0);
    ZMorph.ar(src, morph: morph, shapeA: 0, shapeB: 1) * 0.4;
}.play;
)
x.free;

// 2. Metallic Comb to Bell morph with noise bursts
(
x = {
    var src = PinkNoise.ar(0.3 ! 2);
    var morph = LFTri.kr(0.15).range(0.0, 1.0);
    ZMorph.ar(src, morph: morph, shapeA: 3, shapeB: 4) * 0.5;
}.play;
)
x.free;

// 3. Audio-rate morph modulation
(
x = {
    var src = Pulse.ar(65, 0.25) * 0.3 ! 2;
    var morphMod = SinOsc.ar(80).range(0.0, 1.0);
    ZMorph.ar(src, morph: morphMod, shapeA: 0, shapeB: 4) * 0.4;
}.play;
)
x.free;
::
